       "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/7/8/csm_roboset_software_infodots_de-2_4705ae0232.webp",
       "alt": "",
       "w": 1190,
       "h": 671
      },
      "spots": [
       {
        "x": 30.602,
        "y": 68.234,
        "label": "cutting-edge shape",
        "text": "<h3>cutting-edge shape</h3> <p>The \"Cutting-Edge Shape\" field displays an image of the current cutting-edge shape being used for the measurement. This image serves only to help the operator visualize and identify the cutting-edge shape. A true assistant that makes the user's job easier.</p>"
       },
       {
        "x": 6.586,
        "y": 63.96,
        "label": "Axle Positions",
        "text": "<h3>Axle Positions</h3> <p>The axis positions in »pilot 4.0« of ZOLLER presetting and measuring machines are important reference points that allow users to verify and adjust the exact positioning of the tool or cutting edge. Each axis position represents a specific alignment or position of the tool. By using the axis positions, users can ensure that the tool is correctly positioned and free of deviations, resulting in greater accuracy and efficiency during machining.</p>"
       },
       {
        "x": 68.675,
        "y": 88.462,
        "label": "Function Buttons",
        "text": "<h3>Function Buttons</h3> <p>The function buttons in »﻿﻿﻿﻿pilot 4.0﻿﻿﻿﻿« from ZOLLER serve to enable users to perform the software operation efficiently and to facilitate navigation and the execution of tasks within the software. For example, the function buttons can be used to start tool measurement, load tool data, and exchange views.</p>"
       }
      ],
